          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              quasicoherent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
              of modules
            is the anlog in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
            of the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaf
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
          %p
            A quasicoherent sheaf on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is is equivalently a morphism of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto Mod
            into the canonical stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} : Spec A \mapsto A Mod
            of
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to CRing
            over the category of commutative rings/algebras: this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+category"} tangent category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CRing"} CRing
          %p
            This general abstract description of quasi-coherent sheaves has a fairly direct generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
            over arbitrary
            = succeed "s:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T (C^{op}) \to C^{op}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+fibration"} bifibration
            whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in C^{op}
            plays the role of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            this corresponds to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaf"} (∞,1)-presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
